usage: refine completion [options] bash|zsh|fish

Print shell completion definitions

Options:
  -h, --help                Print this command's help and exit
  -v, --verbose             Describe the request and name the sources read; repeat to trace tool commands
  -q, --quiet               Suppress progress, retaining warnings and errors
  --color VALUE             Diagnostic color: auto (default), always, never
  --diagnostics VALUE       Diagnostic format on standard error: human (default), short, json

Shared options work before or after the command. Values may use
a space or '='. Use '--' before literal operands; @FILE reads
a response file. Single-valued options may be given once.
Of the shared options, lsp takes only --help.

To enable completion in the current shell:
  bash: source <(refine completion bash)
  zsh:  autoload -Uz compinit; compinit
        source <(refine completion zsh)
  fish: refine completion fish | source

